  - PLAYER CHARACTER: printed 50, Hatchling Dragon as an optional Player Character, allows a hatchling of most species (not the Hydra, Cockatrice or Wooly Dragon), with the shared dragon experience table and no starting possessions (starting_money 0, equipment_starting empty). Imported 2026-09-27 on Nate''s decision, in the shape of chiang-ku-dragon: a hatchling and an adult variant, the hatchling first.
  - XP: the Dragon Exp. Table, printed 17, read off a render. The book prints 30 levels; the fifteen lower bounds stored are levels 1-15 (0 to 600,001). Levels 16-30 are recorded on serpent-of-the-wind-dragon.
  - POOLS AND DICE are per variant, as printed. Spd is the running speed; flying is prose. A.R. is prose, as on the Chiang-Ku.
  - ATTACKS: attacks_base per variant, four for the hatchling and eight for the adult; no Hand to Hand style is printed or granted. The attack lines name a fire breath that the entry never describes - recorded as printed.
  - SAVES: "+1 on all other saving throws" (hatchling; +3 adult) is stored on each of the sheet''s d20 saves other than horror factor, which is stated separately. Coma/death is a percentile roll and is left alone.
  - MAGIC AND PSIONICS are the HATCHLING''s, because a variant cannot override either block and the hatchling is the player character. The adult''s are the special abilities above. All wizard spells of levels one and two are granted by name - every catalog spell of levels 1-2 with no tradition whose system is NULL, palladium-fantasy or both (28 on 2026-09-27) - plus Heal Wounds and Blind. Rows added later will not be granted. The 1D4 more from levels 3-4 at even levels is dice-valued, which a spells_schedule count cannot hold, so it is prose in the Magic Knowledge ability (the cats-eye hatchling precedent, and the convention of the other hatchlings imported the same day).
  - PSIONICS: master; seven healing powers plus Psi-Sword by name, two more healing at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12.
  - SKILLS: the R.C.C. list at the adult''s percentages, as printed. The hatchling rule on this page is 96%, not 98%, for languages and basic math, and first-level proficiency for domestic skills, advanced math and all others: the hatchling overrides basic math, Dragonese and Dragonese/Elven literacy to 96, and advanced math and sing to their catalog bases (sing read as a domestic skill, as the book files it). The Language: Other and Literacy: Other picks stay at 98 - an override names a granted skill, not a pick - and their notes say 96 for a hatchling. Literacy in four other languages plus six more spoken is ten Language: Other picks and four Literacy: Other picks (judgement). The picks are written as bonuses on the catalog rows (Language: Other 50 +48, Literacy: Other 30 +68, 98% at first level), because regression refuses a language pick frozen with a base. Ventriloquism and imitate voices and impersonation are natural abilities the book says have skill equivalents; granted as Ventriloquism, Imitate Voices & Sounds and Impersonation at the printed percentages and progression. Recognize and use poison has no catalog row and is prose. Skill proficiency plus I.Q. bonus is the app''s normal rule.
  - The Rifts conversion (three Rifts skills from each of Medical, Science, Pilot, Technical and modern W.P.) is a different system''s stats and is not stored.
  - Alignment (any, but tends toward selfish and evil), size, weight, habitat, life span, enemies and allies are in the body.
